cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Brook in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Brook: TEASAR skeletonization on NVIDIA GPUs"
abstract: >-
  Brook skeletonizes 3D label volumes, such as neuron segmentations in connectomics,
  with the TEASAR algorithm on NVIDIA GPUs (CUDA). It is a drop-in replacement for
  kimimaro.skeletonize: it takes the same arguments and returns osteoid.Skeleton objects.
  Connected components, distance transforms, path tracing and, when memory allows,
  skeleton assembly run on the GPU, for many objects at once and for batches of volumes.
  Brook is a C++17/CUDA library with Python, C and C++ interfaces, for Linux x86-64 and
  NVIDIA GPUs of compute capability 8.0 or newer.
